{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And the priest of</b> — Three times in the Masorah: ולכהן מדין, and twice by the idol of Micah, written לאב ולכהן. Jethro was a priest of idolatry. When Moses married his daughter, Moses needed to vow to him that the first son born to him would be a priest of idolatry. This was his intention, for he knew he would restore his father-in-law to the right path, as he did — for he converted. Nevertheless he was punished, that his grandson became a priest of idolatry, as stated: ויהונתן בן גרשום בן מנשה, and the Sages expounded: he was the son of Moses, only they attribute the corruption to the one who caused it."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "ע\"א is an abbreviation for עבודה זרה (idolatry), resolved from context."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:45.136083168Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}